{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>פוטר</b> — of the language of opening, that is, like one who opens a source of waters that flow and mix with others, until they overwhelm the land; so is the beginning of strife, likened to waters. And before the breaking out, when they have mixed one with the other in strife, it is fitting to abandon the quarrel. Another interpretation: as one who releases waters, so is the beginning of strife — it starts with a little and much comes forth." "<b>התגלע</b> — breaking out."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:22.187501747Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}